  "notes": "Amazon Fire TV 50\" 4K smart TV (AFTTIFF43, codename brandenburg; panel AMZ_K24NE5_4K50M600A),\nFire OS 7.7.1.7 / Android 9 (SDK 28), build PS7717.5741N, MediaTek, armeabi-v7a. US.\nDone remotely over Tailscale through a Synology NAS as subnet router (docs/REMOTE.md, option B).\n\nFIRE OS: DEBLOAT ONLY. Home stays com.amazon.tv.launcher/.ui.HomeActivity_vNext (priority 950);\nthe shared launcher does not apply. Same build line as toshiba-fire-tv-aftha004, and the list\nstarts from it plus the ad and tracking packages from insignia-ns55f301na25.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/amazon-fire-tv-afttiff43/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/amazon-fire-tv-afttiff43/debloat.txt com.amazon.tv.launcher\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nProtected (pm disable-user refused with \"Cannot disable a protected package\"), so left out:\ncom.fireos.usagestats.proxy, com.amazon.device.crashmanager, com.amazon.device.metrics,\ncom.amazon.ftvads.deeplinking.\n\nKept on purpose: Alexa core (com.amazon.vizzini, alexadirectivebrokerservice, alexa.datastore;\nthe Alexa and Fire TV phone apps control the TV through it, and voice only listens while the mic\nbutton is held), casting (AirPlay com.apple.airplay.amazon.airplay, Miracast com.amazon.cast.sink,\nDIAL/whisperplay), OTA updates, Live TV and channel scan, Silk (com.amazon.cloud9) and the website\nlauncher, account and sync services, Appstore, HDMI inputs (com.mediatek.tvinput), remote and\nBluetooth.\n\nShips with only YouTube installed (com.amazon.firetv.youtube); the Netflix/Prime/Disney+ tiles are\nplaceholders that install on first open. The Amazon-hosted hero banner on Home is not affected by\nthis list; Private DNS (dns.adguard-dns.com) works on this build (private_dns_mode hostname) and\nblocks doubleclick.net and amazon-adsystem.com, but not YouTube ads.\n\nadb exec-out screencap -p prints \"Init wrapper sys mutex successful\" before the PNG data on this\nset (docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md).\nContent recognition, telemetry and metrics",
